# Buildr Prompt Management

- Store prompts as `.j2` templates under `packages/core/prompts/`.
- Keep system, mode, tool protocol, repair, and completion-report prompts separate.
- Add a feature/version header comment to every template.
- Define typed template inputs in TypeScript before rendering.
- Cover prompt rendering with golden tests when behavior changes.
- Never concatenate prompts ad hoc inside provider adapters or tool implementations.
- Do not include secrets, raw terminal output, or broad workspace context in docs/provider lookup prompts.
